p(23,20,"York came round to our heads and shortened the rein himself",
 "York shortens the rein by one hole, and Black Beauty finds it hard to go uphill with his head up. Ginger says it is not so bad yet.",
 "York came round to the horses' heads and shortened the rein himself, by one hole, Black Beauty thinks. Every little bit makes a difference, for better or worse, and that day they had a steep hill to go up. Then Black Beauty began to understand what he had heard about. He wanted to put his head forward and pull the carriage up with all his will, as they used to do. But now he had to pull with his head up. That took all the spirit out of him, and the strain came on his back and legs. When they came in, Ginger said, “Now you see what it is like. But this is not bad. If it does not get much worse than this I shall say nothing about it, because we are very well treated here. But if they pull me up tight, they had better take care! I can’t bear it, and I won’t.”",
 ["shortened","strain","steep"])
